<!--
    Phosphor "arrow-left": the same path as ic_ph_arrow_right, mirrored by the group's
    scaleX rather than re-exported, so the two stay identical if the source icon changes.

    The thread header's back button. autoMirrored reads the authored artwork as the
    left-to-right form and mirrors it for RTL, which is the way round this has to be: a back
    arrow points left under English and right under Persian. Pointing the button at
    arrow-right and marking that autoMirrored did the opposite : it left the arrow pointing
    right under English, where it is wrong, and only flipped it under Persian, where it was
    already right. Measured on device, not read: the head's pixel mass sits on the side the
    arrow points at, which is what settles which way a glyph faces.
-->
